whisper.cpp (preferred captions backend)
----------------------------------------
Auto captions prefer the MIT-licensed [whisper.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp)
Windows CLI (`whisper-cli.exe` / `main.exe`) under `whisper\` next to upPlayer, fetched via
`scripts/fetch-whisper-deps.ps1` into `third_party/whisper-win/` (gitignored binaries).

If you redistribute those binaries, keep whisper.cpp’s MIT attribution / LICENSE with the
build (see upstream release package).

Whisper models
--------------
Model files such as `ggml-base.bin` are separate downloads (e.g. Hugging Face
`ggerganov/whisper.cpp`). They are not covered by the upPlayer MIT License; follow the
model provider’s terms.

PotPlayer Whisper module (optional fallback only)
-------------------------------------------------
If no open whisper.cpp CLI is found, upPlayer may fall back to a local PotPlayer
`Module\Whisper` install. Those binaries are proprietary to PotPlayer / Kakao Corp
(or its licensors). They are:

- not part of the upPlayer MIT-licensed codebase
- not redistributed by this repository (gitignored)
- not shipped in upPlayer releases

Do not publish PotPlayer Whisper binaries unless you have permission from the rights holder.

Ultralytics YOLO26 + ONNX Runtime
---------------------------------
Optional object detection uses Ultralytics YOLO26 weights (exported to ONNX) and
Microsoft ONNX Runtime. Those components have their own licenses; they are not
part of the upPlayer MIT-licensed source. Fetch locally with
`scripts/fetch-yolo-deps.ps1` (see `third_party/yolo26/README.md`).

LightFC
-------
Optional single-object tracking uses LightFC (MobileNetV2) weights exported to
ONNX. LightFC and its dependencies have their own licenses; they are not part of
the upPlayer MIT-licensed source. Fetch/export with
`scripts/fetch-lightfc-deps.ps1` (see `third_party/lightfc/README.md`).
